<title>LITHUANIA: PM SAYS EXCISE RATES HIKE TO BOOST INFLATION.</title>
<headline>PM SAYS EXCISE RATES HIKE TO BOOST INFLATION.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's Prime Minister Gediminas Vagnorius said on Thursday that the increase of excise duties on alcohol, tobacco and fuel products will fuel infation and boost it by as much as one percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The inflation pressure from the increase of excise taxes will not exceed one percent,&quot; Vagnorius told a news conference.</p>
<p>Inflation in March was 0.1 percent.</p>
<p>The government forecasts that inflation this year will be between 10 to 12 percent.  </p>
<p>Vagnorius also said that the government expected the excise tariff hikes to add around 310 million litas to the state's coffers this year.</p>
<p>He added that the government would increase excise rates on alcohol and petroleum again but probably not this year.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
